'' WSTR( ) OF AN ENUM LOWERS. 'print wstr( ev )' printed nothing (fbc: 2) and tiko said
'' nothing -- --dump-ir counted it among the statements not lowered, and so did every
'' shape around it: a member, a '&' chain, 'dim as wstring * 20 w = wstr( ev ) & "q"'.
'' Check already typed it (WSTRING * 1, since a6c6a39f); LowerWstrOf (lowerwstrof.bas)
'' then refused the argument as not a BUILTIN. An enum is an INTEGER there now, as
'' NumberToWideTemp_ already had it -- measured, fbc writes 'fb_LongintToWstr( EV$0 )'.
''
'' RUN, because the failure was a missing line: nothing in a dump or a link shows it.
'' The source is also a goldenrun.sh differential -- byte-identical to fbc's build.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/driver/src/wstr-enum.bas -o tests/driver/wstrenum.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/driver/wstrenum.exe
'' RUN: tests/driver/wstrenum.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 2 s1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 2 s2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 2q s3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 2 wz s4
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 1|4000000000|-5|1 s5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: a2b s6
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 4 ln
